                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Delivers on its premise, high on lampshading and humour.\r\n\r\nYou play a villian learning to be a villian and the jokes come from how its plays tropes straight.\r\n\r\nFor example, you pass an exam for \"villian arrogance\" by simply walking out and ignoring the test or your parent will be very proud if you blackmail them into paying your tutation.\r\n\r\nVery funny and ability to choose what kind of villian you want to be, without beeing railroaded into one archtype or god forbid, a hero.",
